 "short_description": "<p>The Intel Core i5 6th Generation Processor family offers desktop computing performance for everyday tasks, office applications, multitasking, and compatible PC upgrades. Specific features, including clock speed, integrated graphics, and power requirements, depend on the exact processor model. Check motherboard compatibility before purchasing.</p>",
 "description": "<p>The Intel Core i5 6th Generation Processor family, based on Intel&#8217;s Skylake architecture, is designed for compatible desktop computers and selected mobile systems. Desktop models can be suitable for office work, everyday computing, web browsing, and entry-level gaming when paired with compatible hardware.</p>\n<p>Depending on the model, these processors offer four cores, Intel Turbo Boost Technology, integrated Intel graphics, and support for compatible DDR4 or DDR3L memory configurations. Performance and available features vary across the product family.</p>\n<p>Before purchasing an Intel Core i5 6th Gen Processor, verify the exact model number, motherboard socket, supported memory type, BIOS compatibility, and cooling requirements. Desktop models generally use the LGA 1151 socket, but compatibility must be checked for the specific motherboard.</p>\n<h4>Product Specifications</h4>\n<div>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Specification</th>\n<th>Details</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Brand</td>\n<td>Intel</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Product Name</td>\n<td>Intel Core i5-6500</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generation</td>\n<td>6th Generation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Processor Family</td>\n<td>Intel Core i5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Architecture</td>\n<td>Skylake</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Product Type</td>\n<td>Desktop Processor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Processor Number</td>\n<td>i5-6500</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lithography</td>\n<td>14 nm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total Cores</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total Threads</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Base Frequency</td>\n<td>3.20 GHz</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum Turbo Frequency</td>\n<td>3.60 GHz</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cache</td>\n<td>6 MB Intel Smart Cache</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bus Speed</td>\n<td>8 GT/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TDP</td>\n<td>65 W</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Socket</td>\n<td>FCLGA1151</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Integrated Graphics</td>\n<td>Intel HD Graphics 530</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graphics Base Frequency</td>\n<td>350 MHz</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graphics Maximum Dynamic Frequency</td>\n<td>1.05 GHz</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory Types</td>\n<td>DDR4-1866/2133, DDR3L-1333/1600 at 1.35 V</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum Memory Size</td>\n<td>64 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory Channels</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum Memory Bandwidth</td>\n<td>34.1 GB/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PCI Express Version</td>\n<td>PCIe 3.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum PCIe Lanes</td>\n<td>16</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Intel Turbo Boost</td>\n<td>Version 2.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hyper-Threading</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Instruction Set</td>\n<td>64-bit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum Supported Displays</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Package Size</td>\n<td>37.5 × 37.5 mm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Thermal Solution Specification</td>\n<td>PCG 2015C (65 W)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div></div>",
